  "notes": "From English \"date.\" In Japanese, デート only refers to romantic outings — never calendar dates ({日付|ひづけ}).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- デートする: to go on a date\n- デートに{行|い}く: to go on a date\n- デートに{誘|さそ}う: to ask someone on a date\n- {初|はつ}デート: first date\n- デートスポット: date spot, romantic location\n\nRELATED EXPRESSIONS:\n- {告白|こくはく}: confession of love (precedes dating in Japan)\n- {付|つ}き{合|あ}う: to go out with, to date (ongoing relationship)\n- {合|ごう}コン: group date/matchmaking party\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nIn Japan, relationships often begin with a {告白|こくはく} (confession) before going on formal dates. デート implies romantic intent.",
